tomization (titles and descriptions)\n2. [](#improved)\n    * Refactored translations to use per-language overrides (thanks to [DSTech-IT](https:\/\/github.com\/DSTech-IT) in [#6](https:\/\/github.com\/pmoreno-rodriguez\/grav-plugin-orestbida-cookie-consent\/pull\/6))\n    * Migrated all modal content to the translations list\n    * Enhanced blueprint structure for better multi-language support\n    * **BREAKING CHANGE**: All customizations must now be done via the `translations` list (classic single-language fields removed)\n    * **BREAKING CHANGE**: `consent_footer` no longer inherits across languages; define it per language as needed\n"},"2.3.3":{"date":"06\/22\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Version number corrected in theme blueprint\n    "},"2.3.2":{"date":"06\/21\/2026","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * Added 1.7|2.0 compatibility flags\n    "},"2.3.1":{"date":"04\/08\/2026","content":"1. [](#bugfix)\n    * fix(core): skip JS injection on non-HTML pages (thanks to [pawellabaj](https:\/\/github.com\/pawellabaj))\n"},"2.3.0":{"date":"02\/14\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Added complete default plugin configuration file with all supported options and sections.\n2. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed fallback consent modal position mapping to `bottom right`.\n3. [](#improved)\n    * Improved Twig JS serialization by using JSON-safe output for configuration strings.\n    * Added missing blueprint fields for `marketing` and `more_info` section content.\n    * Updated plugin metadata and documentation consistency (Composer homepage\/autoload and README config keys).\n"},"2.2.1":{"date":"11\/23\/2025","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * Refactored `onTwigSiteVariables()` method to include hybrid injection.\n    * Optimized `onOutputGenerated()` to detect if script was already rendered before applying fallback.\n2. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fixed Twig template error that unnecessarily redefined `config` variable, causing plugin not to load properly.\n"},"2.2.0":{"date":"10\/13\/2025","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * Improved template security with consistent input sanitization across all user-configurable content\n    * Added `onOutputGenerated` hook to ensure plugin works with all theme configurations\n    * Fixed CDN URLs to use HTTPS instead of HTTP\n"},"2.1.0":{"date":" 03\/22\/2025","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * Updated some translations\n    * Replaced elements type fields with text and textarea fields in the plugin blueprints to improve usability and simplify content management\n    * Added required fields to improve plugin functionality\n2. [](#bugfix)\n    * Fix: Handle null values in escapeQuotes function to prevent type errors\n"},"2.0.1":{"date":" 03\/12\/2025","content":"1. [](#improved)\n    * Updated CDN version\n"},"2.0.0":{"date":" 03\/12\/2025","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Upgraded to the latest version of Orestbida Cookie Consent library (v3.1.0)\n    * Added option `autoShow`: Automatically show the consent modal if consent is not valid\n    * Added option `show_delay` to set the delay in milliseconds before the cookie consent banner is shown\n    * Added option `hideFromBots`: Stops the plugin's execution when a bot\/crawler is detected, to prevent them from indexing the modal's content\n    * Added option `disablePageInteraction`: Creates a dark overlay and blocks the page scroll until consent is expressed\n2. [](#improved)\n    * Refactored the code to make it more maintainable and easier to extend in the future\n    * Updated documentation in README\n"},"1.0.0":{"date":" 01\/30\/2025","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * ChangeLog started..."}}},"facebook-conversion-api":{"name":"Facebook Conversion Api","version":"1.2.0","description":"Facebook Conversion API integration","description_html":"<p>Facebook Conversion API integration<\/p>","description_plain":"Facebook Conversion API integration","icon":"facebook","author":{"name":"Paul Massendari","email":"paulmassendari@pm.me"},"dependencies":[{"name":"grav","version":">=1.7.0"}],"compatibility":{"grav":["1.7","2.0"]},"homepage":"https:\/\/github.com\/paulmassen\/grav-plugin-fbconversionsapi","docs":"https:\/\/github.com\/paulmassen\/grav-plugin-fbconversionsapi\/blob\/main\/README.md","keywords":"grav, plugin, facebook, meta, conversions api, tracking","bugs":"https:\/\/github.com\/paulmassen\/grav-plugin-fbconversionsapi\/issues","license":"MIT","tag_name":"v1.2.0","date":"2026-10-19T09:09:09Z","release_type":"stable","zipball_url":"https:\/\/getgrav.org\/download\/plugins\/facebook-conversion-api\/1.2.0","repository":"https:\/\/github.com\/paulmassen\/grav-plugin-fbconversionsapi","slug":"facebook-conversion-api","install_path":"user\/plugins\/facebook-conversion-api","content_sha256":"34a627b14d1a3b78ae4af19727f0ba8db576191144fd97281486106ebddc9424","changelog":{"1.2.0":{"date":" 10\/19\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Grav 2 and Admin2 compatibility (tested on Grav 2.2.10 + Admin2 2.1.35 \/ API 1.0.51 and Grav 1.7.53.5 + Admin 1.10.60)\n    * Declares `compatibility: grav: ['1.7', '2.0']` so the Grav 2 upgrade preflight and GPM no longer flag the plugin as Grav 1.7 only\n    * `fb_conversion_event()` allowed in sandboxed page content on Grav 2 (`onBuildTwigSandboxPolicy`)\n1. [](#improved)\n    * Visitor IP resolved with `Uri::ip()`, honouring the `system.http_x_forwarded.*` proxy settings\n    * Minimum Grav version raised to 1.7.0\n    * README: Grav 2 \/ Admin2 section, Twig in page content example\n"},"1.1.0":{"date":" 10\/19\/2026","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * Events are queued and sent in `onShutdown`, after the page has been delivered (no more page load delay)\n    * AJAX task `facebookConversion.sendEvent` (e.g. \"Add to calendar\")\n    * `exclude_bots` option (crawlers, scanners, monitoring tools)\n    * `allowed_hosts` option (ignore requests on unknown domains \/ server IP)\n    * `pause_on_error` option: sending is paused after a configuration error (invalid token, missing permission)\n    * `api_version` option (default v25.0)\n    * `fbp` \/ `fbc` cookies and `fbclid` sent for better event match quality\n    * Personal user data (em, ph, fn, ln\u2026) automatically normalized and SHA-256 hashed\n1. [](#improved)\n    * Payload sent as JSON, `test_event_code` only sent when set\n    * No PageView for POST\/HEAD, `.json` requests or error pages\n1. [](#bugfix)\n    * Access token no longer written to the logs\n    * Identical errors logged at most once per hour (log was growing by GB)\n    * Graph API v17.0 (expired) replaced by v25.0\n    * \"Plugin status\" and \"Debug\" labels were swapped in the admin\n    * Debug logging no longer enabled by default when the setting is missing\n    * README: user data must be SHA-256 hashed (not MD5) \u2013 now done automatically by the plugin\n    * Fixed homepage URL and PHP requirement (>= 7.3) in composer.json\n"},"1.0.0":{"date":" 01\/30\/2025","content":"1. [](#new)\n    * ChangeLog started...\n    * Initial Release"}}},"subpages":{"name":"Subpages","version":"1.0.3","description":"Displays a list of direct sub-pages of the current page.","description_html":"<p>Displays a list of direct sub-pages of the current page.<\/p>","description_plain":"Displays a list of direct sub-pages of the current page.","icon":"list-alt","author":{"name":"Andrew Calcutt","email":"acalcutt@techidiots.net"},"homepage":"https:\/\/github.com\/acalcutt\/grav-plugin-subpages","tag_name":"v1.0.3","date":"2025-02-13T14:50:07Z","release_type":"stable","zipball_url":"https:\/\/getgrav.org\/download\/plugins\/subpages\/1.0.3","repository":"https:\/\/github.com\/acalcutt\/grav-plugin-subpages","slug":"subpages","install_path":"user\/plugins\/subpages","content_sha256":"426e9421cc2e365cefa9a4ab2f5ad9085c70cb2ddb23fe1e8e5a91732abb1998","changelog":{"1.0.3\r":{"date":"02\/12\/2025\r","content":"1. [](#fix)\r\n    * Fixed ordered list not working\r\n2. [](#new)\r\n    * Added option to show or hide the previous page link\r\n\r"},"1.0.2\r":{"date":"